// js/infoMap.js - the Info Map registry: every INFORMATION FAMILY the repo holds (not systems, backtests or bots), where it
// lives, how the Desk Terminal uses it, and what a terminal tile could show. Read by the Desk Terminal's Info map tab
// (js/terminal/infoMapView.js), scripts/build_info_map.mjs (derives the rest) and js/infoMap.test.mjs (the guard).
//
// HAND-KEPT here: name, family text, pointers (pages, routes, modules, evidence ids), the traced status and tab, the
// visual idea and the "use" tag. EVERYTHING ELSE is derived by scripts/build_info_map.mjs into js/infoMapDerived.js: whether
// a page or route still exists, last-modified date, Command Hub group, analyst-pack membership, name matches in the terminal /
// Today / Atlas / newsletter code, and each evidence id's verdict word. Run: node scripts/build_info_map.mjs
//
// STATUS is TRACED by reading code (2026-11-13), not a string match: DRAWN = a terminal tab draws the numbers; SUMMARY =
// only a score or one factor of a composite is drawn; PACK = the AI analysts read the feed every morning but the terminal
// draws nothing; STANDALONE = lives on its own page or in an API route only. The generator also name-matches the terminal
// code and flags a row whose status disagrees (a hint to re-trace, never a verdict).
// Evidence: range and timing claims validate, direction claims do not. A null or underpowered id means context only.
// Mark anything not read UNVERIFIED. No em-dashes or arrows in text (the guard test enforces it).

